    <section class="section">
      <div class="shell narrow prose">
        <h2>Our commitment</h2>
        <p>We are committed to protecting people from harm and abuse, responding properly to safeguarding concerns, and making safeguarding everyone’s responsibility. This applies to trustees, volunteers and the partners we work with.</p>

        <h2>Children and adults at risk</h2>
        <p>We recognise our duty of care to children (anyone under 18) and to adults who may be vulnerable, including people living in poverty or in conflict-affected areas. Trustees and partners must complete the appropriate checks before any contact with children. Anyone disqualified from working with children cannot be involved in RallyGood activities.</p>

        <h2>Photography and consent</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>We ask permission before taking or sharing photographs of adults.</li>
          <li>For children, written consent from a parent or guardian is required, stating how the photo will be used.</li>
          <li>Photos must not identify children, or show anyone in a way that could cause harm or distress.</li>
          <li>We do not publish exact locations where that could put people at risk.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Our partners</h2>
        <p>Every partner must demonstrate that it has safeguarding policies and procedures, train its staff, and comply with relevant child protection and adult safeguarding law. We check this before a Drop launches.</p>

        <h2>Raising a concern</h2>
        <p>If you are worried about the safety or welfare of anyone connected with RallyGood, email <a class="text-link" href="mailto:{{EMAIL}}?subject=Safeguarding%20concern">{{EMAIL}}</a>. If someone is in immediate danger, contact the police or the relevant local authority first. Serious concerns are reported to the Charity Commission.</p>

        <p class="small-print">This is a summary. Last updated: October 2026.</p>
      </div>
    </section>
